Consider the gas phase reaction:

CO + \(\frac{1}{2}\) O_{2} ⇌ CO_{2}

At equilibrium for a particular temperature, the partial pressures of CO, O_{2}, and CO_{2} are found to be 10^{-6} atm, 10^{-6} atm, and 16 atm, respectively. The equilibrium constant for the reaction is ______ \times 10^{10} (rounded off to one decimal place).

