Temperatures at two sides of a 0.4 m thick copper plate are 1000 and 500 ℃.

Assuming steady state, one-dimensional conductive heat transfer through the wall and ignoring end-effects, the magnitude of the heat flux through the wall is ______ \times 10^{5} W m^{-2} (in integer).

Given: Thermal conductivity of copper is 400 W m^{-1} K^{-1}

